# Game Texture Editing & Enhancement Suite (`game-texture-editing`)

The `game-texture-editing` skill provides automated, high-precision procedural image processing and repair tools for game development, asset migration, and modding. It allows AI agents and developers to programmatically inspect, enhance, fix, synthesize, and convert textures without opening an interactive GUI editor.

---

## 1. Core Texture Operations Matrix

| Operation | Purpose | Algorithm / Standard | Typical Game Assets |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **`normal-gen`** | Generate 3D surface slope normals | Scharr gradient operator + wrap padding | Wall/ground heightmaps, character fabrics |
| **`normal-blend`** | Combine macro & micro normal maps | Reoriented Normal Mapping (RNM) | Skin pores on face normals, cloth detail on uniforms |
| **`normal-fix`** | Vector normalization, Z-reconstruct, Y-flip | $Z = \sqrt{1 - X^2 - Y^2}$, $G = 1.0 - G$ | DirectX $\leftrightarrow$ OpenGL ports, BC5 fixes |
| **`seamless`** | Eliminate repeating edge seams | 2D Offset wrap + Hermite cross-fade | Terrain ground, tiling bricks, foliage canopies |
| **`alpha-bleed`** | Eliminate dark/white fringe halos | Edge color dilation into $\alpha=0$ | Cutout foliage, hair cards, UI sprites, decals |
| **`delight`** | Strip pre-baked sunlight and shadows | High-pass / Gaussian illumination division | Photographed rock/bark textures $\rightarrow$ PBR Albedo |
| **`sharpen`** | Enhance micro-details without ringing | Contrast-Adaptive Sharpening (CAS) | Blurry upscaled or compressed textures |
| **`pack-pbr`** | Pack 3 single-channel masks into ORM | Red=AO, Green=Roughness, Blue=Metallic | Modern PBR pipelines (Unreal, Unity, Godot) |
| **`stalker-bump`** | Generate paired X-Ray bump textures | Normal+Height (`_bump`) & Gloss (`_bump#`) | S.T.A.L.K.E.R. EE / OGSR Engine modding |
| **`convert`** | Universal format transcode with PoT | Power-of-Two scaling, DXT1/DXT5 compression | DDS, PNG, TGA, WebP asset pipelines |

