## 3. CLI Command Reference (`game-texture-editor`)

Tool executable: `bin/game-texture-editor` (installed to `~/.local/bin/game-texture-editor`).

### 1. Generate Tangent Normal Map
```bash
# Generate DirectX normal map (Green/Y inverted) from diffuse or height image
game-texture-editor normal-gen terrain_diffuse.png -o terrain_normal.dds --strength 3.0 --invert-y --dds dxt5
```

### 2. Blend Base and Detail Normals (RNM)
```bash
game-texture-editor normal-blend character_body_normal.png micro_skin_detail.png -o character_final_normal.dds --dds dxt5
```

### 3. Fix Normal Map Vectors & Flip Y Channel
```bash
# Flip DirectX to OpenGL or reconstruct Z channel from BC5 RG
game-texture-editor normal-fix directx_normal.png -o opengl_normal.png --invert-y
game-texture-editor normal-fix bc5_normal.png -o full_normal.png --reconstruct-z
```

### 4. Synthesize Seamless Repeating Tiling Texture
```bash
game-texture-editor seamless ground_photo.jpg -o ground_seamless.png --feather 0.25
```

### 5. Dilate Alpha Edges (Eliminate Cutout Seam Halos)
```bash
game-texture-editor alpha-bleed foliage_leaf.png -o foliage_leaf_bled.png --steps 8
```

### 6. Strip Baked Lighting (De-light to PBR Albedo)
```bash
game-texture-editor delight bark_photo.jpg -o bark_albedo.png --sigma 30.0
```

### 7. Contrast-Adaptive Sharpening
```bash
game-texture-editor sharpen texture_upscaled.png -o texture_crisp.png --amount 0.8
```

### 8. Pack PBR ORM Texture Map
```bash
game-texture-editor pack-orm --ao ao.png --roughness rough.png --metallic metal.png -o material_orm.dds --dds dxt1
```

### 9. Generate S.T.A.L.K.E.R. Bump Map Pair
```bash
# Generates <texture>_bump.dds (Normal + Height) and <texture>_bump#.dds (Gloss/Error)
game-texture-editor stalker-bump gamedata/textures/wpn/wpn_ak74.dds -o gamedata/textures/wpn/
```

### 10. Transcode Format & Power-of-Two Resizing
```bash
# Resize to nearest Power-of-Two (e.g. 1920x1080 -> 2048x1024) and compress to DXT1 DDS
game-texture-editor convert non_pot_image.png -o game_ready.dds --pot --dds dxt1
```

